---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Git for Statistical Programming | KSM Technology Partners"
  description="Git adoption in pharma statistical programming is no longer optional. KSM helps organizations implement Git with the change management, process design, and programmer buy-in that makes it stick."
>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 1: Hero
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="overline">Git for Statistical Programming</span>
    <h1>Git adoption in statistical programming is no longer optional. Getting it right is.</h1>
    <p>
      Your teams are under pressure to deliver more trials, faster — without compromising GxP compliance.
      Git addresses both. But successful adoption is as much a change management exercise as a technology one,
      and how you implement it determines whether it sticks.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="../contact" class="btn">Talk to a KSM expert</a>
      <a href="#whitepaper" class="btn btn-outline">Read the PHUSE white paper</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 2: The Problem
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="overline">The challenge</span>
        <h2>The decision to adopt Git is easy. Everything after that isn't.</h2>
        <p>
          Git touches every layer of how your statistical programming organization works — from how studies
          and analyses are organized, to how standard macros are shared, to how data flows through your CDR.
          There is no isolated rollout.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3 mt-2">

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="18" cy="18" r="3"/><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="3"/><path d="M13 6h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v7"/><line x1="6" y1="9" x2="6" y2="21"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>It touches everything</h3>
          <p>From SCE integration to QC workflows to data traceability — every implementation decision has downstream consequences. There's no change that doesn't ripple.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>Programmers have to believe in it</h3>
          <p>Without programmer buy-in, adoption fails. Training helps, but it isn't enough. The teams that succeed treat this as a people problem first.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-icon">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.07 4.93A10 10 0 1 0 4.93 19.07"/><path d="M19.07 4.93L12 12"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3>One size does not fit all</h3>
          <p>Branching strategy, commit standards, repository organization, tooling choices — the right answer depends on how your organization actually works, not how a generic implementation guide assumes it does.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 3: Why Now
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="overline">Why now</span>
      <h2>Three forces are making this decision point arrive sooner than most expect.</h2>
      <p>The question is no longer whether your organization will adopt Git — it's whether you do it deliberately, or reactively.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="forces-grid">

      <div class="force-item">
        <div class="force-number">01</div>
        <div class="force-content">
          <h3>Efficiency</h3>
          <p>Manual version control is a compounding tax. Every hour spent tracking down the right file version, reconciling conflicting changes, or reconstructing an audit trail is overhead Git eliminates by design.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="force-item">
        <div class="force-number">02</div>
        <div class="force-content">
          <h3>Vendor independence</h3>
          <p>When your workflows and institutional knowledge are tied to a proprietary SCE, you lose negotiating power and flexibility. Git is open-source, platform-agnostic, and portable. Your intellectual property stays yours.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="force-item">
        <div class="force-number">03</div>
        <div class="force-content">
          <h3>Talent and industry standardization</h3>
          <p>Over 90% of developers use Git. Graduates expect it. Major pharmaceutical companies have already made the transition. Organizations that delay will adopt reactively — with less control and higher switching costs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <blockquote class="pullquote" id="whitepaper">
      <p>"Organizations that move thoughtfully can shape implementation to fit their culture and needs. Those that delay will eventually need to adopt reactively."</p>
      <footer>— <em>The Use of Git in Statistical Programming</em>, PHUSE 2025</footer>
    </blockquote>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 4: The KSM Approach
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="overline">Our approach</span>
        <h2>We've implemented this at major pharmaceutical companies. Here's how we think about it.</h2>
        <p class="intro-para">
          Successful Git adoption requires getting three things right simultaneously.
          Most implementations that struggle have underinvested in at least one of them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="pillars-grid">

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-label">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><line x1="8" y1="21" x2="16" y2="21"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12" y2="21"/></svg>
            Technology
          </div>
          <p>We know the tooling landscape in depth: GitHub vs. GitLab trade-offs including audit log retention for regulatory inspections, SCE integration constraints, CLI vs. GUI adoption considerations, and how to structure repositories for clinical programming workflows. No guesswork.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-label">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="9 11 12 14 22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
            Process
          </div>
          <p>We design the right approach for your ways of working — branching strategy, commit standards, code-to-data traceability, and how Git fits within your existing validation and compliance framework. Not a template. A fit.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="pillar-card">
          <div class="pillar-label">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
            People
          </div>
          <p>Programmer buy-in is the deciding factor. We run these engagements as change management exercises, not technology deployments — involving programmers in decisions that affect their daily work, and building genuine buy-in rather than enforced compliance.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <p class="credibility-line">
        KSM experts are active contributors to the PHUSE Git in Statistical Programming working group and co-authors of the 2025 industry white paper on Git adoption in clinical programming.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 5: Industry Credibility
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="credibility-layout">
      <div class="credibility-badge-col">
        <div class="phuse-badge">
          <div class="phuse-badge-logo">
            <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="phuse-badge-text">
            <span class="phuse-badge-label">PHUSE Working Group</span>
            <span class="phuse-badge-sub">Git in Statistical Programming</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="phuse-badge">
          <div class="phuse-badge-logo">
            <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"/><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div class="phuse-badge-text">
            <span class="phuse-badge-label">White Paper Co-Authors</span>
            <span class="phuse-badge-sub">PHUSE US Connect 2025</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="overline">Industry-recognized expertise</span>
        <h2>Not theoretical advice.</h2>
        <p>
          KSM has implemented Git-based statistical programming workflows at multiple large pharmaceutical companies.
          Our experts co-authored and presented <em>The Use of Git in Statistical Programming</em> at PHUSE US Connect 2025
          — developed through a working group spanning major pharma, CROs, and technology vendors to establish industry best practices.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 6: What Engaging KSM Looks Like
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section">
      <div class="engagement-layout">
        <div>
          <span class="overline">Getting started</span>
          <h2>Where most engagements start.</h2>
          <p>
            We begin with a structured advisory engagement — surfacing where your organization is today,
            what decisions you need to make, and what a realistic adoption path looks like for your specific
            environment, systems, and team. It's a scoped, high-value starting point before any implementation begins.
          </p>
          <p class="no-commitment">No 12-month commitment required to get meaningful clarity.</p>
          <a href="../contact" class="btn mt-2">Talk to a KSM expert</a>
        </div>
        <div class="engagement-steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">1</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Current state assessment</h3>
              <p>We surface where your organization is today — tooling, workflows, programmer workflows, and existing version control practices.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">2</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Decision framework</h3>
              <p>We identify the key decisions your organization needs to make — repository structure, branching model, tooling selection, compliance integration — and the trade-offs at stake.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="step-num">3</div>
            <div>
              <h3>Adoption roadmap</h3>
              <p>You leave with a realistic, sequenced path forward — scoped to your environment, your team, and your regulatory constraints.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Section 7: CTA Block
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="cta-banner">
    <h2>Ready to build a Git adoption approach that actually works for your team?</h2>
    <p>
      Let's talk through where your organization is today and what a realistic path forward looks like.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="../contact" class="btn btn-outline">Talk to a KSM expert &rarr;</a>
      <a href="#whitepaper" class="cta-secondary-link">Download: The Use of Git in Statistical Programming — PHUSE US Connect 2025 &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>

</PageLayout>

<style>
  /* Intro paragraphs */
  .intro-para {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  /* Section heading with lead paragraph */
  .section-heading p {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    max-width: 660px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ---- Forces (Why Now) ---- */
  .forces-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .forces-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .force-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid rgba(178, 209, 234, 0.4);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .force-number {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-blue-pale);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    line-height: 1;
    padding-top: 0.1em;
  }

  .force-content h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-slate);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .force-content p {
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* Pull quote */
  .pullquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-teal);
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-8);
    background: var(--color-teal-light);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-md) var(--radius-md) 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pullquote p {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
    color: var(--color-slate);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .pullquote footer {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  /* ---- Pillars (KSM Approach) ---- */
  .pillars-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .pillars-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .pillar-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid rgba(178, 209, 234, 0.4);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .pillar-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }

  .pillar-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: var(--space-8);
    width: 32px;
    height: 3px;
    border-radius: 0 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--color-blue);
  }

  .pillar-card:nth-child(2)::before { background: var(--color-teal); }
  .pillar-card:nth-child(3)::before { background: var(--color-blue-mid); }

  .pillar-label {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-slate);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .pillar-label svg {
    color: var(--color-teal);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .pillar-card p {
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .credibility-line {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-blue-pale);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* ---- Credibility section ---- */
  .credibility-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .credibility-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 2fr;
    }
  }

  .credibility-badge-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .phuse-badge {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid rgba(178, 209, 234, 0.5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
  }

  .phuse-badge-logo {
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    background: var(--color-teal-light);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--color-teal);
  }

  .phuse-badge-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }

  .phuse-badge-label {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-slate);
  }

  .phuse-badge-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }

  /* ---- Engagement section ---- */
  .engagement-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-12);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .engagement-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .no-commitment {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-teal);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .engagement-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .step {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .step-num {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    background: var(--color-slate);
    color: white;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .step h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-slate);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .step p {
    color: var(--color-slate-gray);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* CTA secondary link */
  .cta-secondary-link {
    color: var(--color-blue-pale);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .cta-secondary-link:hover {
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
</style>
